<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>RFI - All the news from France, Europe, Africa and the rest of the world.</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 08:15:35 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>International</category><title>EU joins aid effort as more than 1,300 remain missing after Nepal floods</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260827-eu-sends-help-as-nepal-flood-kills-165-hundreds-of-tourists-remain-missing</link><description>
The EU has joined international efforts to send aid after catastrophic floods on the Nepal-Tibet border left at least 168 people dead and more than 1,300 missing.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7470e99e-a194-11f1-93c6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-26T134117Z-100630411-RC2D6NA8CH3P-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7470e99e-a194-11f1-93c6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-26T134117Z-100630411-RC2D6NA8CH3P-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">955bd734-a1e1-11f1-98ba-5b8c9d49903f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 06:36:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7470e99e-a194-11f1-93c6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-26T134117Z-100630411-RC2D6NA8CH3P-RTRMADP-3-NEPAL-FLOODS.jpg">© Navesh Chitraka/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Nigerian armed groups net nearly $6m in ransoms: study</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260826-nigerian-armed-groups-net-nearly-6-mn-in-ransoms-study</link><description>
Criminal groups in Nigeria raised nearly $6 million in ransom payments in the last year, a report said Wednesday, with two mass kidnappings by Boko Haram responsible for nearly 90 percent of the total.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/55d8be7a-a195-11f1-b953-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/6961939120bd9f4ef8b93ca57cd743048790f5a8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/55d8be7a-a195-11f1-b953-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/6961939120bd9f4ef8b93ca57cd743048790f5a8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">56fe9964-a195-11f1-a31a-95a8899ba87e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 21:30:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/55d8be7a-a195-11f1-b953-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/6961939120bd9f4ef8b93ca57cd743048790f5a8.jpg">© Ifeanyi Immanuel Bakwenye / AFP/File</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France relaxes rules for three famous cheeses after summer drought</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260827-france-relaxes-rules-for-three-famous-cheeses-after-summer-drought</link><description>
The drought in France is forcing farmers who produce milk for some of the country's most famous cheeses to feed their cows differently, as scorched pastures make it increasingly difficult to stick to strict rules on protected regional foods, known as AOP. Temporary exemptions on fodder sources will apply to the producers of Abondance, Beaufort and Comté to cope with the grass shortage.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a1884fde-2f72-11f0-8e2b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Comte_AOP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a1884fde-2f72-11f0-8e2b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Comte_AOP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bda251f2-a162-11f1-a385-89f34329e939</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 05:16:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a1884fde-2f72-11f0-8e2b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Comte_AOP.jpg">© Wikipédia</source><dc:creator>Alison Hird with RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French PM visits Mayotte to speed up 'slow' reconstruction after cyclone</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260826-french-pm-visits-mayotte-to-speed-up-slow-reconstruction-after-cyclone</link><description>
Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu arrives in the French overseas territory of Mayotte on Wednesday to try to speed up the reconstruction of the archipelago, 18 months after Cyclone Chido caused widespread destruction.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/adc78510-5d78-11f0-9d19-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-64FJ6ZQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/adc78510-5d78-11f0-9d19-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-64FJ6ZQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9efd8954-a12d-11f1-9d4b-c95053c4254a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 10:46:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/adc78510-5d78-11f0-9d19-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-64FJ6ZQ.jpg">© PATRICK MEINHARDT / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French soldiers disciplined over Rhodesian flags linked to white supremacists</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260826-french-soldiers-disciplined-over-rhodesian-flags-linked-to-white-supremacists</link><description>
France's Ministry of the Armed Forces has launched disciplinary proceedings against several soldiers photographed holding flags linked to Rhodesia, a former white minority-ruled territory in southern Africa whose symbols have been embraced by white supremacists.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e9c9d2b2-a08d-11f1-90e8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-88RQ67G.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e9c9d2b2-a08d-11f1-90e8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-88RQ67G.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">be541b62-a162-11f1-b918-37f5a52cec0d</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 16:36:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e9c9d2b2-a08d-11f1-90e8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-88RQ67G.jpg">AFP - LUDOVIC MARIN</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Culture</category><title>From Nashville to Nairobi: Dolly Parton’s enduring African influence</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/culture/20260826-from-nashville-to-nairobi-dolly-parton-s-enduring-african-influence</link><description>
Country music icon Dolly Parton's remarkable career spanned generations and inspired people around the world – including across Africa. The star, who died in Tennessee on Tuesday at the age of 80, was particularly appreciated in South Africa thanks to her collaboration with renowned Zulu group Ladysmith Black Mambazo.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a02dfd6a-a162-11f1-9c09-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Sunny-Holiday-poses-for-a-photo-at-the-Dolly-Parton-mural-in-Nashville-Tennessee-after-her-death-25-Aug-2026-AP-George-Walker-IV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a02dfd6a-a162-11f1-9c09-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Sunny-Holiday-poses-for-a-photo-at-the-Dolly-Parton-mural-in-Nashville-Tennessee-after-her-death-25-Aug-2026-AP-George-Walker-IV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dc4bf2d8-a131-11f1-957a-09b89e57a360</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 16:32:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a02dfd6a-a162-11f1-9c09-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Sunny-Holiday-poses-for-a-photo-at-the-Dolly-Parton-mural-in-Nashville-Tennessee-after-her-death-25-Aug-2026-AP-George-Walker-IV.jpg">AP Photo/George Walker IV - George Walker IV</source><dc:creator>Ollia Horton with RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French prosecutors investigate left-wing mayor over alleged misuse of public funds</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260826-french-prosecutors-investigate-leftwing-mayor-bagayoko-over-alleged-public-funds-misuse-ratp</link><description>
French financial prosecutors have opened an investigation into Bally Bagoyoko, the mayor of Saint-Denis, over suspected misuse of public funds during his employment by the Paris public transport operator RATP when he was also serving as a local elected official with the France Unbowed party. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/92a9f2fc-a05e-11f1-810c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26094612419170.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/92a9f2fc-a05e-11f1-810c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26094612419170.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">307bd96a-a135-11f1-ac41-09b89e57a360</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 13:50:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/92a9f2fc-a05e-11f1-810c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26094612419170.jpg">© Thomas Padilla / AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Nigerian president orders rescue operation after mass kidnapping in mosque</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260826-nigerian-president-tinubu-orders-rescue-operation-after-mass-kidnapping-in-mosque</link><description>
Nigerian President Bola Tinubu has ordered the military and other security agencies to launch an immediate rescue operation after the mass kidnapping of worshippers during an attack on a mosque in the north-central Niger State last week.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fba12020-32fd-11f0-a37e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-04-29T164615Z_786983510_RC2N5X9GBHUH_RTRMADP_3_NIGERIA-SECURITY-MILITARY.JPG"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fba12020-32fd-11f0-a37e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-04-29T164615Z_786983510_RC2N5X9GBHUH_RTRMADP_3_NIGERIA-SECURITY-MILITARY.JPG" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fd076dda-a114-11f1-8d4f-4d9d0ee435e5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 06:19:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/fba12020-32fd-11f0-a37e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-04-29T164615Z_786983510_RC2N5X9GBHUH_RTRMADP_3_NIGERIA-SECURITY-MILITARY.JPG">© REUTERS - Christophe Van der Perre </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>How Dolly Parton became much more than country music’s 'backwoods Barbie'</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260825-how-dolly-parton-became-much-more-than-country-music-s-backwoods-barbie</link><description>
Back in 2008 at age 62, Dolly Parton released a single proclaiming she was "just a backwoods Barbie, too much makeup, too much hair."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/57f47062-a0b1-11f1-bfdf-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/b1eafd7dce9336939880e6ee32dd960e7e66b898.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/57f47062-a0b1-11f1-bfdf-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/b1eafd7dce9336939880e6ee32dd960e7e66b898.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">58e35876-a0b1-11f1-9051-87f52546a6be</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 18:18:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/57f47062-a0b1-11f1-bfdf-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/b1eafd7dce9336939880e6ee32dd960e7e66b898.jpg">© Robyn Beck / AFP/File</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Looking up: Amateur meteorite hunters search for clues to origins of universe</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260826-looking-up-amateur-meteorite-hunters-search-for-clues-to-origins-of-universe</link><description>
French astronaut Sophie Adenot made history this month as the first French woman to perform a spacewalk. Back on Earth, space enthusiasts across France are finding their own ways to reach for the stars. In the third of a five-part series, RFI hears from volunteers in south-west France who are searching for meteorites as part of a citizen science project designed to help researchers recover fragments from space.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/075121dc-a07a-11f1-8b7d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/DSC-0378-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/075121dc-a07a-11f1-8b7d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/DSC-0378-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0560456c-a064-11f1-abeb-db85db5ae3ae</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 13:21:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/075121dc-a07a-11f1-8b7d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/DSC-0378-1.jpg">© Baptiste Coulon / RFI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>'Shocking' book about Putin's private life wins French literary prize</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260825-shocking-book-about-putin-s-private-life-wins-french-literary-prize</link><description>
A taboo-breaking book about Vladimir Putin's rise to power and private life, written by two exiled Russian journalists, won a newly established French literary prize on Tuesday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1da653fe-8530-11f1-b1cb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T164544Z-2032476191-RC2LHMAO5MSC-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-PUTIN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1da653fe-8530-11f1-b1cb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T164544Z-2032476191-RC2LHMAO5MSC-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-PUTIN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">56adb7b2-a09e-11f1-8d4d-b97a63a72a51</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 16:02:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1da653fe-8530-11f1-b1cb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-20T164544Z-2032476191-RC2LHMAO5MSC-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-PUTIN.jpg">via REUTERS - Alexander Kazakov</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Namibia to rebury remains of political prisoners returned by South Africa</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260826-namibia-to-rebury-remains-of-political-prisoners-returned-by-south-africa</link><description>
Two Namibian colonial-era political prisoners, whose remains were returned by South Africa last week, are to be reburied in Namibia as part of Wednesday’s Heroes Day ceremonies. They are among a group of Namibians who died in South Africa under apartheid or during the colonial period and whose remains have been repatriated.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bd65cd3e-12a5-11ea-9736-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/2018-08-29t085135z_888509700_rc1fa2e0d7c0_rtrmadp_3_germany-namibia_0.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bd65cd3e-12a5-11ea-9736-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/2018-08-29t085135z_888509700_rc1fa2e0d7c0_rtrmadp_3_germany-namibia_0.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">83ec8b5a-9c9c-11f1-8280-f5365118855f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 04:55:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bd65cd3e-12a5-11ea-9736-005056a99247/w:1024/p:16x9/2018-08-29t085135z_888509700_rc1fa2e0d7c0_rtrmadp_3_germany-namibia_0.jpg">© Christian Mang/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Environment</category><title>France says US risks ‘blocking everything’ at UN talks to protect world’s soils</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/environment/20260825-france-says-us-risks-blocking-everything-at-un-talks-to-protect-world-soils-cop17-desertification</link><description>
The soil that grows the world's food and holds its water is becoming less productive, yet governments are struggling to agree on how to respond to this crisis. As political talks at Cop17, the United Nations conference on desertification and land degradation, stepped up in Mongolia on Tuesday, France's environment ambassador Barbara Pompili warned that disputes involving the United States are threatening progress. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/25db6fc2-a098-11f1-a9d6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP22305010588451.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/25db6fc2-a098-11f1-a9d6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP22305010588451.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2868478e-a097-11f1-9bbb-23fdf51191ba</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 15:59:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/25db6fc2-a098-11f1-a9d6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP22305010588451.jpg">AP - Rafiq Maqbool</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France's Sophie Adenot returns to the void for second spacewalk in a week</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260825-french-astronaut-sophie-adenot-to-make-second-spacewalk-to-finish-repairs</link><description>
French astronaut Sophie Adenot on Tuesday stepped outside the International Space Station (ISS) for the second time, a week after she became the first French woman to perform a spacewalk. Adenot and US astronaut Anil Menon are due to finish replacing a faulty antenna on the ISS after running out of time during their first spacewalk on 18 August.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c386df8a-9fc2-11f1-b73a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-18T193750Z-1637559858-RC211NAFX3V1-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-SPACEWALK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c386df8a-9fc2-11f1-b73a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-18T193750Z-1637559858-RC211NAFX3V1-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-SPACEWALK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d50039fa-9fc2-11f1-b33b-e347e9354ddc</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 05:57:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c386df8a-9fc2-11f1-b73a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-18T193750Z-1637559858-RC211NAFX3V1-RTRMADP-3-SPACE-SPACEWALK.jpg">via REUTERS - NASA</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Survivors of Guinea's deadly landfill collapse say authorities ignored warnings</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260825-survivors-of-guinea-s-deadly-landfill-collapse-say-authorities-ignored-warnings</link><description>
Two days after a deadly landfill collapse in Guinea, rescuers are using giant excavators to search for victims. Anger is rising among residents, who say they had warned authorities that the rubbish dump was precarious.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7284eb0e-9f36-11f1-b23d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6BN4GG.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7284eb0e-9f36-11f1-b23d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6BN4GG.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4c158146-a06b-11f1-a6a2-f1db79bccd1e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 12:10:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7284eb0e-9f36-11f1-b23d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6BN4GG.jpg">AFP - -</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>US and Denmark push for nationwide expansion of UN arms embargo in Sudan</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260825-us-and-denmark-push-for-nationwide-expansion-of-un-arms-embargo-in-sudan</link><description>
The United States on Monday urged the United Nations Security Council to expand an arms embargo on the Sudanese region of Darfur to cover all of Sudan, saying the nation's brutal conflict risks regional expansion. The suggestion was supported by Denmark, which holds the Council's rotating presidency. 
